# Medusa (20158), every draw 0: her attacked hook reads her hit points before the hit lowers
# them. The first hit (850 of her 1000) finds her at full hit points and hating no one, so only
# her parent's attacked hook answers it. The second finds her at 150 (15%, under a fifth), hit
# by the creature she hates most: she calls out (NpcString 1000452). She also asks for her
# fatal poison (4320-3) on the character, which the scenario's skill table does not hold, so no
# cast desire is queued here; tests/ai/warrior_individual1c_test.go checks that desire.
character Hunter 20
random always 0
script script.ai.individual.DefaultNpc
script script.ai.individual.Monster.MonsterAI
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.WarriorBase
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.Warrior
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.WarriorAggressive.WarriorAggressive
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.WarriorAggressive.Medusa
npc medusa 20158 Monster 40 0 0

hit medusa 360
  desires medusa attack(player)=4500
hit medusa 10
  S NpcSay obj=medusa type=0 npc=1020158 text="It's a good day to die! Welcome to hell, maggot!"
  desires medusa attack(player)=4625
